## What search engines may read

To keep the Worker''s CPU time within its allowance, crawlers are invited to a bounded set of pages: the fixed pages, the fleet''s cars, the landing pages, the guides, and the vehicle pages down to the trim (/cars/make/model/year/trim). The place pages, the colour pages, the search term pages (/t/), the /buy pages and the detailing and body shop place pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap. A crawler that asks anyway gets a short refusal before the site loads.

From 70% of the month''s included CPU time, crawlers get no catalog page at all ("try again tomorrow") until the month resets. People always get every page.

## IndexNow

**Search**, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own; a refusal waits an hour, then longer. Sweep: the priority list once a week; a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row.
