-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: &quot;Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons&quot;. The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet&#39;s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked &quot;not the exact year&quot;; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b>. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pick again</b> asks for the next best photo; <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show stock photos</b> in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer&#39;s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Quality gate: off. On, only places within the delivery reach are in search, and rental pages only with a real matching car. Search engines can treat many similar pages as low value; the gate lowers that risk.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: every province, state and territory is on. Untick a region to take its pages and sitemaps off the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term (its pages then leave search), switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages say plainly that CarmaCars does not sell, finance or lease cars; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. CarmaCars does not do this work, and the pages say so: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-what-search-engines-may-read" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What search engines may read</h2><p class="gd-p">To keep the Worker&#39;s CPU time within its allowance, crawlers are invited to a bounded set of pages: the fixed pages, the fleet&#39;s cars, the landing pages, the guides, and the vehicle pages down to the trim (/cars/make/model/year/trim). The place pages, the colour pages, the search term pages (/t/), the /buy pages and the detailing and body shop place pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap. A crawler that asks anyway gets a short refusal before the site loads.</p><p class="gd-p">From 70% of the month&#39;s included CPU time, crawlers get no catalog page at all (&quot;try again tomorrow&quot;) until the month resets. People always get every page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-indexnow" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">IndexNow</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b>, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own; a refusal waits an hour, then longer. Sweep: the priority list once a week; a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'usage-and-paid-usage', 'chapter', 'assistant', 'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do** and one email to the alert address. When it is used up, a second card and email.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.
', 'Usage and paid usage', 'Included allowances, the 80% and used-up alerts, Workers AI by feature (never paid), allowing paid usage for photos, what pauses and what never does.',
  'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do** and one email to the alert address. When it is used up, a second card and email.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.

## Alerts by text and the banner

7. When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website''s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).
8. While a figure is at its warning level or past it, a banner at the top of **Today** says so: red past the allowance, amber before.

## Emails through Cloudflare first

9. The site''s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. "Emails this month (Cloudflare)" counts them. It needs the one-time setup in docs/changes/2026-11-03-cloudflare-email.md.
10. "Texts this month (Quo)" counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (**Change the allowance**).
',
