/h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Usage</b>: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app&#39;s own record shows as Unmetered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the shares</b> to change the assistant&#39;s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the allowance</b> after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Database size and file storage are our own server&#39;s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-alerts-by-text-and-the-banner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts by text and the banner</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="7"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website&#39;s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">While a figure is at its warning level or past it, a banner at the top of <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> says so: red past the allowance, amber before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-emails-through-cloudflare-first" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Emails through Cloudflare first</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="9"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">The site&#39;s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. &quot;Emails this month (Cloudflare)&quot; counts them. It needs the one-time setup in docs/changes/2026-11-03-cloudflare-email.md.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Texts this month (Quo)&quot; counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (<b class="gd-ui">Change the allowance</b>).</div></li></ol></div></section>');
